2186435355 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435355 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435355 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435355 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435355 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cb94596e-e304-53f4-bc22-e71a468af9b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435358 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435358 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111501" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435358 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435358 #edb/ref 1071 "The matrix $W$ is given below. Let ${w}_{1}$, ${w}_{2}$, and ${w}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $W.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{w}_{1},{w}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(W).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${w}_{2}={x}_{1}{w}_{1}+{x}_{3}{w}_{3}.$\n\n$$\nW=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -9 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435358 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa6c549b-f344-52f9-9015-63f22befbecb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435358 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we reduce the matrix $W$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -9 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{20}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(W)$ is $\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{3}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $2$nd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${w}_{2}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{w}_{2}}={{(-3)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{w}_{1}}+{{(0)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{w}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}=(-3)\\cdot 0=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435359 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0a6387a3-d6c3-514a-adf3-03c92255b693" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435359 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435360 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435360 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "56aac62a-1ac3-595b-9746-f6129816ec3d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435360 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435361 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435361 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "83ebb46d-c1c6-5af5-a88b-0a90f6597d01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435361 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435362 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435362 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96ef3e91-81f5-56af-9b4b-af5a3c54255c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435362 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186345143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435363 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435363 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "af78af8e-c58a-51c1-8a5d-a8deb9557dbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186435363 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435357 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
